1
00:00:00,507 --> 00:00:01,913
Oh my gosh, guys!

2
00:00:02,062 --> 00:00:04,155
Finally, you came to visit!

3
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:07,187
- Our Gen-Z friends are complete!
- Right?!

4
00:00:14,463 --> 00:00:16,603
I really miss our high
school days, don’t you?

5
00:00:16,628 --> 00:00:17,416
Yeah!

6
00:00:17,441 --> 00:00:18,935
Oh my gosh, I have so much gossip for you!

7
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,433
Oh? What happened? Tell me!

8
00:00:20,458 --> 00:00:21,077
Wait, wait, wait!

9
00:00:21,102 --> 00:00:25,289
Before you start gossiping, order lots of
food so we can make good sales, okay?

10
00:00:26,562 --> 00:00:27,428
You’re treating me!

11
00:00:27,453 --> 00:00:28,192
I’ll treat you!

12
00:00:28,217 --> 00:00:28,779
Yeah, it’s on you!

13
00:00:28,928 --> 00:00:30,355
Ah, hello!

14
00:00:30,627 --> 00:00:31,574
Guys, hang on a sec.

15
00:00:31,599 --> 00:00:33,514
- Okay, okay.
- Alright!

16
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:34,898
Lola?

17
00:00:35,728 --> 00:00:36,815
It’s hot!

18
00:00:37,365 --> 00:00:38,139
Oh, oh!

19
00:00:38,164 --> 00:00:40,456
Oh, hello, Lola!

20
00:00:40,534 --> 00:00:41,660
Oh no!

21
00:00:42,925 --> 00:00:47,098
Look at you all, you’ve grown so much!

22
00:00:47,123 --> 00:00:51,605
Do you remember the ensaymada
you used to bring to school?

23
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:53,757
Well, it’s still a bestseller! Look!

24
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,906
- Wow!
- Wow!

25
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:58,013
Guys, wait.

26
00:00:58,591 --> 00:01:02,198
Lola, how many grams
of sugar does this have?

27
00:01:02,418 --> 00:01:03,892
And how many calories?

28
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,399
Sugar? Calories? What’s
that? How should I know?

29
00:01:07,603 --> 00:01:08,831
You know what, let’s check!

30
00:01:08,856 --> 00:01:09,900
Yeah, let’s check!

31
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:21,728
Oh my gosh, Lola. One
piece is 100 calories?

32
00:01:22,525 --> 00:01:26,331
That’s 39 minutes of walking
or 11 minutes of jogging.

33
00:01:26,356 --> 00:01:28,186
Nope, no thanks! I’ll pass!

34
00:01:28,211 --> 00:01:30,966
- Pass, we pass!
- Sorry, pass, it’s not gonna do.

35
00:01:30,991 --> 00:01:32,923
Pass? Pass?!

36
00:01:33,298 --> 00:01:38,576
You little—are you eating this, or
do you want to take a nap instead?!

37
00:01:38,808 --> 00:01:40,534
- We’re eating, we’re eating!
- Yeah, we’re eating!

38
00:01:40,805 --> 00:01:41,799
We’re eating.

39
00:01:41,824 --> 00:01:44,184
- Cheers!
- Cheers! Cheers!

40
00:01:44,315 --> 00:01:46,261
Don’t make your Lola mad!

41
00:01:46,631 --> 00:01:47,632
Sorry.

42
00:02:48,106 --> 00:02:49,300
- Iskineport…
- Mmm?

43
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,033
Don’t you have anywhere
to go for Christmas?

44
00:02:52,308 --> 00:02:53,152
Nope.

45
00:02:54,095 --> 00:02:55,072
- No?
- Yes.

46
00:02:55,097 --> 00:02:56,465
No one loves you?

47
00:02:57,464 --> 00:02:58,498
No – no one!

48
00:02:58,523 --> 00:02:59,795
Do you have someone
who loves you?

49
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,011
Where are you spending Christmas?

50
00:03:01,036 --> 00:03:02,323
Just here.

51
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,131
No one loves me either.

52
00:03:04,156 --> 00:03:06,964
Wow, you ask as if I’m
the only one who’s unloved.

53
00:03:06,989 --> 00:03:08,417
My Christmas is gonna be so cold.

54
00:03:09,965 --> 00:03:11,285
- Psst, hey!
- Mmm?

55
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,983
What are you two talking about?

56
00:03:13,008 --> 00:03:15,942
No one loves you? What’s that about?

57
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:19,697
We don’t have anywhere to go for
Christmas, no family, no one loves us.

58
00:03:19,722 --> 00:03:20,972
What do you call us, then?

59
00:03:21,553 --> 00:03:23,026
Aren’t we your family?

60
00:03:23,718 --> 00:03:25,705
We love you so much, you know that.

61
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:27,793
This is your home, you belong here.

62
00:03:27,956 --> 00:03:30,747
If you don’t have anywhere
to go for Christmas, stay here.

63
00:03:30,772 --> 00:03:32,588
We’ll spend it together.

64
00:03:32,703 --> 00:03:34,703
- Thanks, Kuya.
- Of course!

65
00:03:35,053 --> 00:03:36,613
You guys are like…

66
00:03:37,701 --> 00:03:39,461
See? Sounds like a better
idea to stay here, right?

67
00:03:43,575 --> 00:03:45,482
Oh, is it okay here?

68
00:03:46,734 --> 00:03:47,641
I don’t know!

69
00:03:47,666 --> 00:03:51,409
You know, sometimes I
think about going to SpaKarl!

70
00:03:51,434 --> 00:03:51,842
Huh?

71
00:03:51,867 --> 00:03:52,323
Yeah!

72
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:53,504
- Why?
- I just want to go there!

73
00:03:53,675 --> 00:03:54,321
You’re really going there?

74
00:03:54,346 --> 00:03:55,168
Yeah, why not?

75
00:03:55,541 --> 00:03:56,361
Don’t!

76
00:03:56,386 --> 00:03:57,469
Why not?!

77
00:03:57,618 --> 00:03:58,984
That place isn’t for you!

78
00:03:59,066 --> 00:04:00,559
- You have a wife and kids!
- Exactly.

79
00:04:00,584 --> 00:04:01,856
I’m not gonna do anything bad—

80
00:04:01,978 --> 00:04:03,525
I just want a massage!

81
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:05,668
- Ate Cha is gonna be mad at you!
- Oh, Kuya.

82
00:04:05,693 --> 00:04:07,838
She can’t get mad at me.

83
00:04:07,863 --> 00:04:11,080
I’m the king here, I make the decisions!

84
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:17,916
They trust me, I’ll do what
I want, and I’ll pay for it!

85
00:04:17,941 --> 00:04:19,647
- That’s on you, Kuya, okay?
- It really is on me!

86
00:04:19,672 --> 00:04:21,267
Hmmm? What did you say?

87
00:04:21,401 --> 00:04:24,441
- Uh-oh. You said that’s on you.
- My love…

88
00:04:25,001 --> 00:04:26,140
What did you say?

89
00:04:26,165 --> 00:04:27,046
Nothing.

90
00:04:27,071 --> 00:04:29,877
Sometimes I just feel like
banging my head against the wall.

91
00:04:31,761 --> 00:04:32,947
I don’t know anymore.

92
00:04:37,754 --> 00:04:39,947
Oooooh!

93
00:04:40,449 --> 00:04:42,016
Hey, stop that!

94
00:04:42,302 --> 00:04:43,502
There’s nothing between us!

95
00:04:44,066 --> 00:04:45,773
"Nothing"?!

96
00:04:46,894 --> 00:04:48,534
Oh really? Want me to spill the tea?

97
00:04:48,559 --> 00:04:49,639
Hep!

98
00:04:49,903 --> 00:04:51,303
You’re good right where you are!

99
00:04:51,328 --> 00:04:53,086
Whatever! Alright, you’re Orbs!

100
00:04:53,303 --> 00:04:55,916
What’s this? It’s too early for gossip!

101
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:58,453
Same old Tso K—still salty!

102
00:04:59,790 --> 00:05:01,491
How about I sprinkle salt
on your mouth instead?

103
00:05:01,943 --> 00:05:03,816
Tso K-Tso K, salty-salty!

104
00:05:04,746 --> 00:05:07,599
Well, lucky you’re here because
I have something for you to do.

105
00:05:09,456 --> 00:05:10,870
Do you know Don Al?

106
00:05:11,151 --> 00:05:12,584
You mean Donald Duck?

107
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:17,714
Excuse me, it’s Don Al Buff-Dak.

108
00:05:18,547 --> 00:05:19,700
Don Al Dak.

109
00:05:19,862 --> 00:05:20,811
Again.

110
00:05:21,370 --> 00:05:24,584
Dol Al Buff-Dak.

111
00:05:25,305 --> 00:05:26,172
Donald Duck?

112
00:05:26,197 --> 00:05:28,306
You mean the rich guy who
owns the balut business?

113
00:05:28,331 --> 00:05:29,277
Extremely rich.

114
00:05:29,302 --> 00:05:30,533
Yes!

115
00:05:30,558 --> 00:05:36,585
So here’s the deal—Don Al wants to
hold an inter-barangay parol contest.

116
00:05:36,859 --> 00:05:41,840
He wants our barangay to win
so we can boost business here!

117
00:05:43,006 --> 00:05:46,493
And I’m willing to support your project.

118
00:05:47,471 --> 00:05:49,745
No matter how much it
costs, I’ll cover everything.

119
00:05:50,038 --> 00:05:51,644
Wow!

120
00:05:51,669 --> 00:05:53,277
That’s amazing!

121
00:05:53,302 --> 00:05:55,032
This guy really knows how to brag.

122
00:05:55,057 --> 00:05:56,083
Excuse me, what did you say?

123
00:05:56,108 --> 00:05:57,507
Uh, nothing!

124
00:05:57,532 --> 00:06:00,459
I said you’re so handsome
and so generous.

125
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,439
- Super generous!
- The most generous!

126
00:06:02,464 --> 00:06:04,647
Give me the peso. Peso, now!

127
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,928
Here you go, kid.

128
00:06:06,270 --> 00:06:07,130
Really?

129
00:06:07,155 --> 00:06:09,483
Money for you and your friends,
go buy yourselves some drinks.

130
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:10,436
Okay?

131
00:06:10,461 --> 00:06:12,718
- That’s crazy!
- Soft drinks?!

132
00:06:12,743 --> 00:06:14,126
I just want you to know,

133
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:19,330
whatever amount you need
for this project—sky’s the limit.

134
00:06:21,965 --> 00:06:23,212
That’s a lot!

135
00:06:23,241 --> 00:06:26,011
Oh right, call my daughter.
Daphne!

136
00:06:26,318 --> 00:06:27,138
Oh right, call my daughter.
Daphne!

137
00:06:31,352 --> 00:06:32,292
Hi, Dad!

138
00:06:32,317 --> 00:06:32,819
Hi.

139
00:06:33,329 --> 00:06:37,510
Uh, guys, I want you to meet
my daughter—Daphne Dak.

140
00:06:39,074 --> 00:06:39,821
Something funny?

141
00:06:39,871 --> 00:06:41,825
Oh, nothing! Nothing!

142
00:06:43,368 --> 00:06:47,181
- Hi, hello! Nice to meet you!
- Uh, hi!

143
00:06:47,301 --> 00:06:48,161
Hi, Daphne!

144
00:06:50,951 --> 00:06:53,525
Ah-ah–Andres. Pers.

145
00:06:53,670 --> 00:06:55,936
Andres? Nice name!

146
00:06:56,011 --> 00:06:58,551
Is it just me or is this short?

147
00:06:59,914 --> 00:07:02,614
Kuya, I think Daphne is in love with you.

148
00:07:03,474 --> 00:07:05,107
There’s something there.

149
00:07:05,132 --> 00:07:07,311
Yeah, Andres! Go for it!

150
00:07:07,336 --> 00:07:09,879
Who wouldn’t want to
date someone rich, right?

151
00:07:09,927 --> 00:07:12,527
Hey! Hey, hey, hey!

152
00:07:13,271 --> 00:07:14,354
What do you mean go for it?

153
00:07:14,937 --> 00:07:16,152
What do you mean rich?

154
00:07:16,177 --> 00:07:18,450
You think my Orb is just after money?!

155
00:07:18,475 --> 00:07:23,025
Whoa, calm down, little miss jealous!

156
00:07:24,549 --> 00:07:26,256
Come on, guys, maybe
she’s just being friendly.

157
00:07:27,242 --> 00:07:29,297
Just because she’s nice
doesn’t mean she likes me.

158
00:07:31,481 --> 00:07:34,822
Hi, Andres! How are you?

159
00:07:34,847 --> 00:07:35,889
Hi! Hello!

160
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:37,222
You look tired.

161
00:07:37,247 --> 00:07:38,850
Poor thing!

162
00:07:39,023 --> 00:07:42,133
I’m here, don’t get sick, okay?
I’ll take care of you, don’t worry!

163
00:07:42,158 --> 00:07:45,357
Wait, wait, wait, hold on.
Daphne, why are you here?

164
00:07:45,862 --> 00:07:51,212
Oh, Dad told me to come here because
he’s giving the money for the lanterns.

165
00:07:51,237 --> 00:07:54,718
Wait, why didn’t he just bring it himself?

166
00:07:54,917 --> 00:07:57,291
Andres, you’re handsome,
but you’re kinda slow!

167
00:07:57,316 --> 00:08:00,447
Obviously, so I could see you!

168
00:08:00,763 --> 00:08:03,376
Don’t you want to see me? I know you do!

169
00:08:04,049 --> 00:08:06,880
- Hey! Hold up, hold up, hold up!
- Hooray!

170
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:13,092
Excuse me, but could you stop
getting all up in my Orb’s face?

171
00:08:14,562 --> 00:08:15,508
Are you his girlfriend?

172
00:08:15,715 --> 00:08:16,861
Huh? No.

173
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:18,774
Oh, then go back to your place!

174
00:08:18,799 --> 00:08:20,693
Shoo, shoo, shoo!

175
00:08:21,384 --> 00:08:22,484
Are you okay?

176
00:08:25,442 --> 00:08:27,849
- Sis, hi, sis!
- Sis!

177
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:31,017
Sis!

178
00:08:31,590 --> 00:08:33,397
Are you okay? Want
me to help you with that?

179
00:08:33,947 --> 00:08:35,420
Hi, boys!

180
00:08:35,445 --> 00:08:37,233
- Hi!
- You up for a massage?

181
00:08:37,710 --> 00:08:40,110
How much? We might
not be able to afford it.

182
00:08:40,165 --> 00:08:41,618
- We can afford it!
- Really?

183
00:08:41,686 --> 00:08:46,326
Actually, it’s cheap! We
have a Christmas promo!

184
00:08:46,351 --> 00:08:46,745
Nice!

185
00:08:46,770 --> 00:08:49,236
- Thirty-minute massage…
- Okay?

186
00:08:49,261 --> 00:08:51,348
- Only 499 pesos.
- Wow!

187
00:08:51,435 --> 00:08:55,215
- Plus, free one hour massage!
- Okay!

188
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:58,857
- Sounds good!
- Wait! What are you saying?!

189
00:08:58,917 --> 00:09:00,050
Tso K, you said—

190
00:09:00,732 --> 00:09:01,419
Wrong!

191
00:09:01,658 --> 00:09:07,050
I said a thirty-minute massage,
then a one-hour foot massage!

192
00:09:07,278 --> 00:09:08,171
Oh, still a massage!

193
00:09:08,386 --> 00:09:09,819
Foot massage! Foot!

194
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:13,914
And don’t even bother with
those two! They don’t have money!

195
00:09:13,939 --> 00:09:14,367
Wow!

196
00:09:14,392 --> 00:09:16,515
That’s harsh, Tso K! We have money!

197
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:19,619
- Oh, really? Where’d you get it?
- It’s Christmas time!

198
00:09:19,644 --> 00:09:22,490
Ugh! We just got our salary! This?

199
00:09:22,515 --> 00:09:24,097
This 1,000 peso bill is just spare change!

200
00:09:24,330 --> 00:09:26,914
- We even dropped our dollars earlier.
- Wow, really?!

201
00:09:26,946 --> 00:09:27,467
Of course!

202
00:09:27,492 --> 00:09:29,151
Oh, so you do have money! Then come on in!

203
00:09:29,176 --> 00:09:31,939
A while ago, you were shooing us
away, and now that you see our money—

204
00:09:31,964 --> 00:09:33,043
No, I was just joking!

205
00:09:33,234 --> 00:09:35,534
Give it here. Oh yeah,
you gave 1,000, right?

206
00:09:35,559 --> 00:09:37,576
I’m keeping the change, okay?
Come on in.

207
00:09:37,942 --> 00:09:38,926
Okay!

208
00:09:39,806 --> 00:09:41,427
Oh!

209
00:09:41,452 --> 00:09:41,898
What is this?

210
00:09:41,923 --> 00:09:42,983
- What took you so long to come out?!
- Iskineport!

211
00:09:43,008 --> 00:09:45,027
We’re about to get in,
and now you’re coming out?

212
00:09:45,091 --> 00:09:46,571
Are you guys getting a massage too?

213
00:09:46,596 --> 00:09:47,387
Yeah!

214
00:09:47,412 --> 00:09:48,906
Oh, let’s all go together!

215
00:09:48,931 --> 00:09:50,447
One room for all of us!

216
00:09:51,013 --> 00:09:54,346
Why all together?! No way,
this feels like a horror house!

217
00:09:54,371 --> 00:09:56,514
- Come on, come on!
- Let’s go!

218
00:09:56,539 --> 00:09:59,663
Go in, you’re already paid!

219
00:09:59,688 --> 00:10:00,264
Come on!

220
00:10:00,289 --> 00:10:03,677
Just go in! You’re already
paid, so go in! Don’t be scared!

221
00:10:03,702 --> 00:10:06,121
It’s not scary! Lights on, lights on!

222
00:10:18,363 --> 00:10:19,443
Yes, Dad?

223
00:10:20,049 --> 00:10:22,962
Wow! My daughter is so beautiful!

224
00:10:23,019 --> 00:10:25,910
- It’s nothing!
- Andres isn’t here yet?

225
00:10:26,056 --> 00:10:27,796
Mmm, he’s on his way, Dad.

226
00:10:28,150 --> 00:10:29,271
Mmm.

227
00:10:29,542 --> 00:10:30,952
You smell extra nice today.

228
00:10:30,977 --> 00:10:33,663
I could smell you two blocks away!

229
00:10:33,688 --> 00:10:36,265
Of course, Dad! Gotta be
fresh when Andres gets here!

230
00:10:36,582 --> 00:10:38,975
You know, Dad, I really
have a crush on him.

231
00:10:39,441 --> 00:10:40,740
You have a crush on him?

232
00:10:41,547 --> 00:10:43,440
What’s happening to your taste, sweetie?

233
00:10:43,465 --> 00:10:45,518
Your eyesight’s getting worse!

234
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:49,318
Our family is full of good-looking people.

235
00:10:49,583 --> 00:10:51,123
And yet, your crush is ugly?

236
00:10:51,154 --> 00:10:52,548
Dad, that’s so mean!

237
00:10:53,013 --> 00:10:54,546
He’s really handsome!

238
00:10:54,753 --> 00:10:56,725
- You think that’s handsome?
- Yes!

239
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:59,113
Ugh, I don’t get you! Anyway…

240
00:10:59,138 --> 00:11:00,364
Dad, just let me be!

241
00:11:00,389 --> 00:11:04,479
My heart doesn’t beat like this
often. Okay? Just support me.

242
00:11:05,251 --> 00:11:09,348
Fine, I support you, but
very important reminder…

243
00:11:09,573 --> 00:11:10,698
Yes, Dad?

244
00:11:10,723 --> 00:11:16,595
In our family, marriage comes
first before…you give up the goods.

245
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:20,073
Dad, seriously?! I’m conservative, okay!

246
00:11:20,672 --> 00:11:21,978
- Just remember that!
- Okay!

247
00:11:22,634 --> 00:11:25,473
I’m only saying this because

248
00:11:28,673 --> 00:11:30,986
I love you, and you know that.

249
00:11:31,171 --> 00:11:32,524
Yes, I know, Dad.

250
00:11:32,929 --> 00:11:36,962
I’d do anything to protect you, okay?

251
00:11:37,889 --> 00:11:38,906
I love you!

252
00:11:38,931 --> 00:11:40,471
I think you need this too, Dad.

253
00:11:43,576 --> 00:11:44,962
- But it’s good!
- Good, right?

254
00:11:44,987 --> 00:11:45,989
Smells nice?

255
00:11:46,308 --> 00:11:47,195
All good now.

256
00:11:47,352 --> 00:11:51,018
Remember, a wedding
before you give up the goods.

257
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:52,284
Okay, okay!

258
00:12:03,647 --> 00:12:04,703
Hello?

259
00:12:05,373 --> 00:12:06,766
Yes, Andres? Hello?

260
00:12:08,966 --> 00:12:10,206
Oh, you’re here?

261
00:12:10,779 --> 00:12:11,482
Okay, okay!

262
00:12:11,507 --> 00:12:17,870
Just go up to the second floor, turn
right, go straight, and that’s my room.

263
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:20,917
Yes, see you!

264
00:12:21,629 --> 00:12:23,649
Okay, bye!

265
00:12:27,783 --> 00:12:29,069
Oh, breath spray!

266
00:12:30,629 --> 00:12:31,462
Daphne?

267
00:12:31,487 --> 00:12:33,320
- Oh, hi, Andres!
- Uh, good evening!

268
00:12:33,610 --> 00:12:34,564
Good evening!

269
00:12:34,589 --> 00:12:35,603
Why are we meeting here?

270
00:12:36,205 --> 00:12:37,589
You guys have a living room.

271
00:12:37,614 --> 00:12:42,839
Yes, I know, but it’s better here in
my room! Lots of pictures, and privacy!

272
00:12:43,037 --> 00:12:44,537
Oh, okay?

273
00:12:55,459 --> 00:12:58,592
Uh, sure. But I just came to
get the money for the lanterns.

274
00:12:59,305 --> 00:13:00,392
Oh, really?

275
00:13:00,838 --> 00:13:01,919
Okay, okay.

276
00:13:02,418 --> 00:13:02,911
Sure, sure.

277
00:13:02,978 --> 00:13:04,831
Uh, sit down first. Sit down.

278
00:13:05,070 --> 00:13:05,650
Okay!

279
00:13:05,675 --> 00:13:06,878
I’ll call Dad.

280
00:13:06,903 --> 00:13:07,418
Okay.

281
00:13:07,443 --> 00:13:08,630
Feel at home, okay?

282
00:13:08,816 --> 00:13:10,020
Okay.

283
00:13:11,863 --> 00:13:12,709
Whoa!

284
00:13:12,734 --> 00:13:13,127
Hi!

285
00:13:13,218 --> 00:13:14,545
Whoa, you’re suddenly here?!

286
00:13:14,570 --> 00:13:15,638
Oh man.

287
00:13:16,275 --> 00:13:17,466
Sorry, sorry.

288
00:13:17,639 --> 00:13:18,809
I think there was a blackout.

289
00:13:19,913 --> 00:13:20,784
Oh!

290
00:13:20,816 --> 00:13:23,290
Oh no! This is scary!

291
00:13:25,393 --> 00:13:26,393
Gotcha!

292
00:13:28,431 --> 00:13:30,044
What are you doing to my daughter?!

293
00:13:30,195 --> 00:13:31,628
Nothing! Nothing! I swear!

294
00:13:31,653 --> 00:13:33,669
Nothing?! Look at the two of you!

295
00:13:51,269 --> 00:13:52,976
Dad, let him go already.

296
00:13:53,473 --> 00:13:56,606
The sun’s up! I’m sure
his family is looking for him.

297
00:13:57,518 --> 00:13:58,594
Let him go?!

298
00:13:59,284 --> 00:14:02,111
He’s lucky he even
lived to see the sunrise!

299
00:14:02,136 --> 00:14:03,151
I’m being nice!

300
00:14:03,872 --> 00:14:05,078
It’s simple—

301
00:14:05,815 --> 00:14:08,761
marry my daughter or
I’ll shut down your store!

302
00:14:08,944 --> 00:14:12,683
P-please, no! That’s my
family’s livelihood, please!

303
00:14:12,896 --> 00:14:14,556
Alright. Now, stand up.

304
00:14:15,549 --> 00:14:16,077
Stand up.

305
00:14:16,102 --> 00:14:18,048
Dad, just let him go home.

306
00:14:18,518 --> 00:14:19,480
Why?

307
00:14:19,505 --> 00:14:21,192
He still needs to change!

308
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:22,693
Mmm…

309
00:14:23,944 --> 00:14:25,367
Raise your right hand.

310
00:14:26,862 --> 00:14:30,582
Do you swear to marry
my daughter, Daphne?

311
00:14:33,317 --> 00:14:34,063
Yes.

312
00:14:36,989 --> 00:14:38,256
Here’s your change.

313
00:14:38,281 --> 00:14:39,765
- Thank you, Lola.
- Come back again!

314
00:14:51,591 --> 00:14:53,758
Chard, finish the juice, don’t waste it!

315
00:14:57,729 --> 00:14:59,516
Ah, so good! Oh?

316
00:15:00,676 --> 00:15:01,809
I’ll take this to the kitchen.

317
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:02,860
The kitchen?

318
00:15:04,452 --> 00:15:06,385
Hi, Iskineport!

319
00:15:06,865 --> 00:15:07,978
See you later, okay?

320
00:15:09,871 --> 00:15:12,484
Really? Okay, let’s all
meet up there, Muffins!

321
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:19,116
Are we getting a massage later?
We don’t have money anymore!

322
00:15:19,141 --> 00:15:21,687
Shh! Don’t be so loud!

323
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:24,124
- Ow, ow!
- There’s Kuya Aga!

324
00:15:29,296 --> 00:15:31,356
Looks like you guys had a little
too much fun last night, huh?

325
00:15:33,381 --> 00:15:39,475
My love, there’s nothing wrong
with relaxing and unwinding. It’s fine!

326
00:15:40,113 --> 00:15:41,139
Thanks, Ate Cha!

327
00:15:41,170 --> 00:15:44,082
Wait—why is it okay
for them but not for me?!

328
00:15:44,411 --> 00:15:45,481
Nope.

329
00:15:45,838 --> 00:15:46,838
You’re too weak.

330
00:15:47,271 --> 00:15:48,151
That’s it.

331
00:15:48,176 --> 00:15:49,603
You give in too easily!

332
00:15:51,165 --> 00:15:52,785
Well, there’s your reason, Kuya Aga!

333
00:15:54,033 --> 00:15:55,600
Go ahead! Push through with it!

334
00:15:55,661 --> 00:15:58,101
- Don’t go with them!
- Oh, I’m not going!

335
00:15:58,126 --> 00:15:59,583
Exactly, so stay here.

336
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:01,000
Alright, we’re heading back!

337
00:16:01,059 --> 00:16:03,432
Okay, we’ll just bring this along!

338
00:16:03,457 --> 00:16:06,061
- Well, don’t drink it and then return it!
- Oh, sorry! Right!

339
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,687
I’m just gonna rough him
up inside—he’s too noisy!

340
00:16:10,346 --> 00:16:11,392
Iskineport!

341
00:16:11,783 --> 00:16:13,596
Tell me about it later, okay?!

342
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:15,700
Tell you about what?

343
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:17,984
Wait a minute! I noticed something.

344
00:16:19,482 --> 00:16:23,276
Atasha, it looks like Andres
didn’t go home last night.

345
00:16:24,053 --> 00:16:25,513
I didn’t see him.

346
00:16:25,796 --> 00:16:26,967
Did you?

347
00:16:27,343 --> 00:16:28,563
Mom, my lips are sealed.

348
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:30,287
What do you mean, “my lips are sealed”?!

349
00:16:31,046 --> 00:16:34,066
Look at you, your reaction says it all—

350
00:16:34,214 --> 00:16:35,608
Oh, there he is!

351
00:16:36,601 --> 00:16:37,624
See?!

352
00:16:42,028 --> 00:16:43,828
Hey, Andres.

353
00:16:48,399 --> 00:16:50,079
Looks like you didn’t
go home last night, huh?

354
00:16:50,871 --> 00:16:54,318
That outfit—you were
wearing that the other day.

355
00:16:55,677 --> 00:16:57,243
Did you sleep somewhere else?

356
00:16:57,647 --> 00:16:58,961
That doesn’t look good.

357
00:17:00,658 --> 00:17:01,704
Dad, Mom…

358
00:17:02,128 --> 00:17:03,375
- What?!
- Something happened.

359
00:17:03,421 --> 00:17:04,556
- Huh?!
- What?!

360
00:17:04,581 --> 00:17:05,741
What do you mean something happened?!

361
00:17:05,766 --> 00:17:08,311
Wait! Okay, calm down, calm down!

362
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:09,702
What happened?!

363
00:17:10,233 --> 00:17:11,436
An accident, Dad.

364
00:17:11,659 --> 00:17:12,772
- An accident?
- An accident?!

365
00:17:13,569 --> 00:17:15,369
- Huh?! What?!
- What accident?!

366
00:17:15,394 --> 00:17:16,538
Did you get hurt?!

367
00:17:16,962 --> 00:17:18,063
No, Grandma.

368
00:17:18,088 --> 00:17:19,139
It’s just…

369
00:17:19,466 --> 00:17:20,516
I’m getting married.

370
00:17:20,541 --> 00:17:21,774
- What?!
- What?!

371
00:17:21,799 --> 00:17:22,819
What?!

372
00:17:29,714 --> 00:17:30,687
Traitor!

373
00:17:35,678 --> 00:17:41,066
But yeah, that’s why I
have to marry Daphne.

374
00:17:41,332 --> 00:17:42,449
Huh?!

375
00:17:43,125 --> 00:17:44,352
Marry her, Andres?!

376
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,040
Where is Andres?!

377
00:17:46,493 --> 00:17:47,026
Huh?!

378
00:17:47,051 --> 00:17:48,763
What did you do to my nephew?!

379
00:17:48,788 --> 00:17:49,768
I’m gonna hurt you!

380
00:17:49,793 --> 00:17:50,468
Come here!

381
00:17:50,493 --> 00:17:52,114
- Let me go!
- Tso K!

382
00:17:52,152 --> 00:17:54,126
Let me go! That hurts!

383
00:17:54,872 --> 00:17:56,272
Let me go!

384
00:17:56,866 --> 00:17:57,813
What is this?!

385
00:17:57,838 --> 00:17:58,941
BFF!

386
00:17:59,007 --> 00:17:59,919
BFF!

387
00:17:59,944 --> 00:18:00,531
BFF.

388
00:18:00,556 --> 00:18:01,878
BFF!

389
00:18:01,954 --> 00:18:04,147
Calm down! Calm down!

390
00:18:04,354 --> 00:18:05,968
Anne is crying!

391
00:18:06,774 --> 00:18:08,694
- Why? What happened?
- Anne is crying.

392
00:18:08,719 --> 00:18:10,001
Explain properly.

393
00:18:10,026 --> 00:18:13,972
My nephew is crying,
and I feel bad for her.

394
00:18:14,208 --> 00:18:18,197
It’s because Don Al wants
Andres to marry Daphne

395
00:18:18,234 --> 00:18:22,223
‘cause he thinks something
happened between them!

396
00:18:22,897 --> 00:18:23,912
Oh?

397
00:18:24,890 --> 00:18:26,147
But that’s a good thing!

398
00:18:27,091 --> 00:18:28,225
She’s rich!

399
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:29,605
He should marry her!

400
00:18:29,630 --> 00:18:31,777
At least you guys can pay me back!

401
00:18:31,802 --> 00:18:34,432
Wait, wait, hold on!

402
00:18:34,773 --> 00:18:38,670
This conversation is getting
messier—let’s all calm down!

403
00:18:39,227 --> 00:18:43,868
Andres, grandson, if nothing
happened, then nothing happened.

404
00:18:44,544 --> 00:18:50,430
And if you’re going to marry her, it should
be because you love her, not because…

405
00:18:50,674 --> 00:18:55,231
you have to, even if you don’t want to!

406
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:58,770
Lola Maxi is right!

407
00:18:59,265 --> 00:19:00,372
Everything—

408
00:19:00,969 --> 00:19:03,229
- hold on, let me explain. Okay?
- I got you.

409
00:19:04,708 --> 00:19:09,975
Everything can be
talked about calmly, right?

410
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:10,484
Right.

411
00:19:10,509 --> 00:19:11,317
- Right?
- Yeah.

412
00:19:11,342 --> 00:19:12,344
That’s possible.

413
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:13,707
- Dad…
- Huh?

414
00:19:13,808 --> 00:19:14,766
Dad…

415
00:19:15,068 --> 00:19:16,825
Huh? I’m just gonna talk to my son.

416
00:19:16,850 --> 00:19:19,246
Wait, wait. Don’t
just—he might get injured.

417
00:19:19,271 --> 00:19:20,370
Look at me, I
already have an injury.

418
00:19:20,395 --> 00:19:23,847
- Tso K, Tso K, Tso K!
- Hold on. What? What is it?

419
00:19:24,051 --> 00:19:25,759
Andres was held at gunpoint.

420
00:19:25,784 --> 00:19:26,410
Ha?!

421
00:19:26,435 --> 00:19:27,674
- He was what?!
- Shotgun!

422
00:19:27,699 --> 00:19:30,939
Shotgun?! What shotgun?!

423
00:19:31,529 --> 00:19:33,397
Wait a minute, that’s not okay!

424
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:34,334
Andres!

425
00:19:34,359 --> 00:19:35,393
You were held at gunpoint?!

426
00:19:35,512 --> 00:19:36,765
I can’t let that slide!

427
00:19:36,790 --> 00:19:38,123
- Oh, hold on!
- I can’t let that slide!

428
00:19:38,148 --> 00:19:41,746
Stop it! Just calm down!
Don’t get all worked up!

429
00:19:42,623 --> 00:19:43,672
BFF!

430
00:19:44,665 --> 00:19:48,498
Calm down, my love.
What we need is a solution!

431
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:49,937
- Oh!
- Oh!

432
00:19:50,363 --> 00:19:51,657
We have a solution!

433
00:19:52,067 --> 00:19:58,717
Meet and greet—tada! Andres 2.0!

434
00:19:58,742 --> 00:19:59,812
There he is!

435
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:02,136
Andres, is that you?!

436
00:20:02,295 --> 00:20:04,555
No! He’s Jen Mulach!

437
00:20:12,265 --> 00:20:17,012
My love! We have a big problem.

438
00:20:18,535 --> 00:20:20,948
We really have a problem with Andres!

439
00:20:21,432 --> 00:20:23,232
Aside from that.

440
00:20:24,493 --> 00:20:25,362
There's more?!

441
00:20:25,387 --> 00:20:26,278
Mmm.

442
00:20:26,303 --> 00:20:28,677
The sales are way too short!

443
00:20:29,712 --> 00:20:31,525
We got robbed!

444
00:20:32,153 --> 00:20:34,433
We got robbed? How did that happen?

445
00:20:34,788 --> 00:20:38,775
How is the money short when I'm
always there watching the cash register?

446
00:20:39,826 --> 00:20:42,626
Oh, so what happened to the
money? Did it just magically disappear?

447
00:20:42,736 --> 00:20:45,195
Thieves are different these days!

448
00:20:45,289 --> 00:20:46,436
They're really good!

449
00:20:46,955 --> 00:20:49,289
Ugh, it's almost Christmas!

450
00:20:57,893 --> 00:20:58,914
I got it.

451
00:20:59,179 --> 00:20:59,947
What?

452
00:20:59,972 --> 00:21:01,085
I'll take care of this.

453
00:21:01,998 --> 00:21:03,398
I'll handle it.

454
00:21:15,578 --> 00:21:16,432
Oh, what’s that?

455
00:21:18,273 --> 00:21:21,573
Orb, are you sure Daphne isn’t here?

456
00:21:22,125 --> 00:21:23,296
Of course!

457
00:21:23,392 --> 00:21:24,330
I swear!

458
00:21:24,355 --> 00:21:27,818
That’s why I’m dressed
like this, so no one recognizes me.

459
00:21:27,928 --> 00:21:30,172
Iskineport’s
idea is genius, right?

460
00:21:30,916 --> 00:21:32,349
Hi, Andres!

461
00:21:32,388 --> 00:21:33,467
Hi, Andres!

462
00:21:34,388 --> 00:21:35,775
Hey, Andres!

463
00:21:35,801 --> 00:21:36,787
Wow!

464
00:21:36,812 --> 00:21:38,572
Looking good!

465
00:21:38,778 --> 00:21:40,158
Rock and roll!

466
00:21:40,542 --> 00:21:42,656
What’s the occasion? Is
there a costume party, Andres?

467
00:21:42,681 --> 00:21:43,994
You recognize me?

468
00:21:44,019 --> 00:21:45,295
Well, of course!

469
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,400
You look exactly like yourself!

470
00:21:46,428 --> 00:21:48,012
Even like Tash over here!

471
00:21:48,037 --> 00:21:49,378
You’re totally you!

472
00:21:51,057 --> 00:21:52,323
Hey, guys!

473
00:21:52,348 --> 00:21:55,242
Hi, Tash! Hi, Andres!

474
00:21:55,267 --> 00:21:56,491
What happened to you?

475
00:21:57,101 --> 00:21:58,295
You recognize me?

476
00:21:58,652 --> 00:22:00,692
You guys, seriously! You ditched us, huh?

477
00:22:00,717 --> 00:22:02,458
But here, the Christmas lantern is done.

478
00:22:02,483 --> 00:22:04,566
Wow! It’s beautiful!

479
00:22:04,688 --> 00:22:05,780
Have you tested it yet?

480
00:22:05,974 --> 00:22:06,983
Not yet.

481
00:22:07,156 --> 00:22:09,763
Boss Beauty, can we test it?

482
00:22:09,788 --> 00:22:10,693
Can we plug it in?

483
00:22:10,725 --> 00:22:17,923
Oh, that lantern? This one? Yeah, sure.
Sure. I thought it was already good to go.

484
00:22:18,267 --> 00:22:20,934
- Here we go, here we go, here we go.
- Alright, let’s go!

485
00:22:20,959 --> 00:22:23,179
Careful, okay? You might get electrocuted!

486
00:22:23,665 --> 00:22:26,058
One, two, three!

487
00:22:30,267 --> 00:22:32,193
You sneaky little—!

488
00:22:32,713 --> 00:22:34,566
No wonder my electricity
bill is through the roof!

489
00:22:34,591 --> 00:22:36,432
You’re all plugging into my place!

490
00:22:42,516 --> 00:22:43,593
I do.

491
00:22:43,814 --> 00:22:44,860
Yes, I do.

492
00:22:48,329 --> 00:22:49,381
Come in.

493
00:22:54,144 --> 00:22:57,364
So you’re the jealous one
who’s not even the girlfriend.

494
00:22:58,174 --> 00:23:03,991
Daphne, I just want to ask
you—please, don’t do this to Orb.

495
00:23:05,341 --> 00:23:07,769
Sorry, but he has no choice.

496
00:23:07,794 --> 00:23:11,241
We’re getting married.
We’re forever, no matter what.

497
00:23:13,085 --> 00:23:16,645
But did something really
happen between you two?

498
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:18,993
Us? Something happened?

499
00:23:19,057 --> 00:23:20,837
Of course not!

500
00:23:20,905 --> 00:23:23,185
I’m conservative, okay?!
My parents are strict!

501
00:23:23,773 --> 00:23:26,116
So you really just set him up?

502
00:23:27,439 --> 00:23:33,333
Mmm, set-up, shotgun, forced
wedding—call it what you want.

503
00:23:33,358 --> 00:23:36,147
I don’t care because we’re
getting married for real.

504
00:23:36,184 --> 00:23:38,351
Forever. We are forever. Okay?

505
00:23:38,544 --> 00:23:42,388
Alright then, goodbye, good night.
I need my beauty rest. Babush!

506
00:23:42,495 --> 00:23:45,205
See you tomorrow at
the wedding! Bye-bye!

507
00:23:47,727 --> 00:23:49,507
See you tomorrow, Andres!

508
00:24:03,404 --> 00:24:09,020
Muffin is amazing! All the
tension in my body is gone!

509
00:24:09,718 --> 00:24:12,984
But why does it look like
you’ve got boils on your thigh?

510
00:24:13,009 --> 00:24:14,353
- Violet?
- Yeah!

511
00:24:14,690 --> 00:24:18,947
That’s just the lighting!
And she gives the best massages!

512
00:24:19,335 --> 00:24:21,315
- We should come back here!
- Seriously, back pain gone, right?

513
00:24:21,340 --> 00:24:24,878
Sounds like our boss! Oh… Kuya Aga!

514
00:24:25,512 --> 00:24:26,532
Feels great, huh?

515
00:24:26,711 --> 00:24:27,351
Yeah.

516
00:24:27,376 --> 00:24:29,246
But… but… you guys are
getting massages too often.

517
00:24:29,863 --> 00:24:30,776
That’s expensive!

518
00:24:30,801 --> 00:24:31,735
Yeah.

519
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:32,874
It feels amazing, but still!

520
00:24:32,918 --> 00:24:34,291
Only in moderation.

521
00:24:34,335 --> 00:24:35,388
Yeah, moderation.

522
00:24:35,413 --> 00:24:38,073
- If you can afford it, then sure, go back.
- So, you’re saving up for this?

523
00:24:38,808 --> 00:24:39,469
Yeah.

524
00:24:39,494 --> 00:24:40,134
This is from your savings?

525
00:24:40,159 --> 00:24:41,551
We’ve been setting money
aside for this, Kuya Aga.

526
00:24:41,576 --> 00:24:42,431
You didn’t skim changes from the store?

527
00:24:42,456 --> 00:24:43,286
Hey!

528
00:24:43,311 --> 00:24:44,401
No way!

529
00:24:44,426 --> 00:24:45,819
We don’t steal!

530
00:24:46,981 --> 00:24:52,988
Kuya, are you accusing
us of stealing from you?

531
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:56,300
How could I not? It’s expensive!

532
00:24:56,743 --> 00:24:58,990
So, you’re really sticking to that, huh?
You didn’t take anything?

533
00:24:59,263 --> 00:25:00,569
No! We’re not like that!

534
00:25:00,622 --> 00:25:01,682
You ever see us steal?

535
00:25:01,759 --> 00:25:02,639
Even just a piece of bread—

536
00:25:02,664 --> 00:25:04,221
Iskineport, Iskineport!

537
00:25:04,272 --> 00:25:07,499
You really had to bring
your busted piggy bank here!

538
00:25:09,013 --> 00:25:10,353
That money came from a piggy bank?

539
00:25:11,582 --> 00:25:13,797
Dude, let’s go eat at Bake Haus of U again!

540
00:25:13,934 --> 00:25:15,996
Lola Maxi always
gives us excess change.

541
00:25:16,293 --> 00:25:18,511
Yeah, we always save
money there! Let’s go!

542
00:25:25,097 --> 00:25:27,144
Lola Maxi gives extra change?

543
00:25:27,992 --> 00:25:35,705
Wait, wait, wait, wait… Ah, Iskineport,
Chard, I’m really sorry, okay?

544
00:25:38,693 --> 00:25:40,106
I mean it.

545
00:25:40,524 --> 00:25:41,497
Sorry.

546
00:25:42,214 --> 00:25:44,594
Kuya, that really hurts.

547
00:25:44,619 --> 00:25:52,016
We work hard, we save up just to relax, and
then you accuse us of stealing from you.

548
00:25:52,041 --> 00:25:54,578
Didn’t you say we’re family?

549
00:25:54,603 --> 00:25:57,266
It’s just… you guys were the only ones I
noticed… But sometimes, yeah, I was wrong.

550
00:25:58,311 --> 00:25:59,818
I was wrong, wrong, wrong.

551
00:26:00,477 --> 00:26:02,623
Can you just help me
with Lola Maxi instead?

552
00:26:03,413 --> 00:26:06,320
Let’s go to the bakeshop and
help her out. I’m really sorry.

553
00:26:06,455 --> 00:26:07,975
Come to think of it, Lola
Maxi is confused, too.

554
00:26:08,115 --> 00:26:08,575
Exactly.

555
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:12,810
She’s 137 years old already.
She should be resting.

556
00:26:12,869 --> 00:26:14,696
That’s why her eyesight is so bad, huh?

557
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:16,693
Alright, we’ll go.

558
00:26:16,718 --> 00:26:19,130
We’ll take care of
Lola Maxi and the shop.

559
00:26:19,194 --> 00:26:20,174
Okay, thanks.

560
00:26:20,199 --> 00:26:21,198
Are you getting a massage?

561
00:26:21,223 --> 00:26:23,033
I’ll stay here… No, I’ll stay here.

562
00:26:23,058 --> 00:26:24,737
I want to try it.

563
00:26:24,810 --> 00:26:26,363
Does Ate Cha know about this?

564
00:26:27,136 --> 00:26:28,323
Does she have to?

565
00:26:28,560 --> 00:26:30,653
Kuya, get number nine!

566
00:26:30,806 --> 00:26:31,973
They’re really good!

567
00:26:34,816 --> 00:26:36,163
You sure, Kuya Aga?

568
00:26:36,219 --> 00:26:37,249
You’re really getting a massage?

569
00:26:37,274 --> 00:26:40,126
Hey, if I can? I mean,
I’ll pay for it myself, right?

570
00:26:40,205 --> 00:26:41,505
Alright then, Kuya Aga!

571
00:26:41,530 --> 00:26:44,200
Oh, by the way, also here is—

572
00:26:45,806 --> 00:26:53,315
It feels so good! The best! So
relaxing! Look, my neck pain is gone!

573
00:26:53,340 --> 00:26:55,108
- Gone! Yay!
- Feels great!

574
00:26:55,133 --> 00:26:56,479
- You got a massage?!
- Of course!

575
00:26:56,808 --> 00:27:00,936
I had to try it! Look! Oh…
Man, I feel so—Let’s go home.

576
00:27:00,961 --> 00:27:02,828
Wait! Wait! Kuya Aga, weren’t
you gonna get a massage?

577
00:27:02,853 --> 00:27:04,022
Me? Did I say that?

578
00:27:04,047 --> 00:27:06,147
Yeah, you just said you were
getting one. You literally just—

579
00:27:06,172 --> 00:27:06,985
You said that?

580
00:27:07,010 --> 00:27:08,775
No! Why would I do that?
That’s a waste of money!

581
00:27:09,759 --> 00:27:11,273
Ah… ah, okay.

582
00:27:11,298 --> 00:27:13,118
My wife is here! That’s a waste of money!

583
00:27:13,143 --> 00:27:16,678
Ah, alright, let’s go home! I’ll give
you a massage instead, my love!

584
00:27:18,725 --> 00:27:23,462
Andres! Andres! Andres!

585
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,393
Oh, my!

586
00:27:24,418 --> 00:27:27,809
Didn’t I tell you to marry
my daughter?! Huh?!

587
00:27:27,834 --> 00:27:30,113
- Cha! Cha! Cha!
- Ahh! Wait a minute!

588
00:27:30,138 --> 00:27:32,360
Hey, hold on, hold on!

589
00:27:32,641 --> 00:27:35,441
Uh… excuse me, sir, who are you?

590
00:27:36,503 --> 00:27:37,623
You don’t know me?!

591
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:45,148
I’m Don Al-Dak! Don Al-Dak!

592
00:27:45,542 --> 00:27:47,015
- Don Al-Dak?
- Yes!

593
00:27:47,055 --> 00:27:51,205
Don Al-Dak, excuse me,
but there won’t be a wedding.

594
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:53,725
Wow, you’ve got some nerve!
Why?! Who do you think you are?!

595
00:27:53,750 --> 00:27:55,690
I’m Andres’s father.

596
00:27:56,516 --> 00:27:58,276
Why won’t there be a wedding?

597
00:27:58,302 --> 00:28:01,082
This isn’t right! You can’t
just force a shotgun wedding!

598
00:28:01,228 --> 00:28:02,773
And marriage, just like that?!

599
00:28:03,008 --> 00:28:04,881
They barely even know each other!

600
00:28:04,925 --> 00:28:05,445
Exactly!

601
00:28:05,473 --> 00:28:08,374
What is this, like rice? If it’s
too hot, you just spit it out?!

602
00:28:08,846 --> 00:28:12,917
Of course, I’m a father. I was hurt when
I saw something happen between them!

603
00:28:12,942 --> 00:28:14,208
Nothing even happened!

604
00:28:14,233 --> 00:28:15,101
What do you mean "noth—"

605
00:28:15,126 --> 00:28:16,253
Dad, stop it!

606
00:28:16,278 --> 00:28:17,386
Let’s just start the wedding!

607
00:28:17,411 --> 00:28:20,290
- Come on…
- Wait! Wait!

608
00:28:25,119 --> 00:28:29,533
Daphne, I just want to ask
you, please, don’t do this to Orb.

609
00:28:29,853 --> 00:28:32,280
Sorry, but he doesn’t have a choice.

610
00:28:32,316 --> 00:28:35,670
We’re getting married.
We’re forever, no matter what.

611
00:28:36,380 --> 00:28:39,693
But… did something really
happen between you two?

612
00:28:40,715 --> 00:28:42,987
Us? Something happened? Of course not!

613
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:46,147
I’m conservative! My parents are strict!

614
00:28:46,782 --> 00:28:49,015
So, you just set him up?

615
00:28:49,226 --> 00:28:53,341
Yep, set up, shotgun,
forced—call it whatever you want,

616
00:28:53,365 --> 00:28:57,481
I don’t care, because we’re
getting married tomorrow.

617
00:29:00,127 --> 00:29:02,293
You?! How dare you!

618
00:29:02,524 --> 00:29:05,630
Checkmate! Nothing
happened between you two.

619
00:29:08,434 --> 00:29:09,491
Sorry, Dad.

620
00:29:09,995 --> 00:29:12,455
I’m sorry, everyone. I
just really love Andres.

621
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:14,361
But what you did was wrong.

622
00:29:14,766 --> 00:29:16,952
You’re ruining our family’s name.

623
00:29:18,148 --> 00:29:22,687
To all of you, Mr. and
Mrs. Pers, I-I apologize.

624
00:29:22,966 --> 00:29:26,439
I just acted on impulse because, of course,
I just wanted to protect my daughter…

625
00:29:26,471 --> 00:29:31,554
I understand. As a parent, I know what
a father goes through for his daughter.

626
00:29:31,980 --> 00:29:32,741
Okay?

627
00:29:32,766 --> 00:29:37,289
I sincerely apologize to all of
you. I apologize, I’m really sorry.

628
00:29:37,707 --> 00:29:39,615
- Andres, I’m sorry.
- Mr. Don Al, it’s okay.

629
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,440
But, Daphne,

630
00:29:44,373 --> 00:29:47,467
you know, love isn’t just
something you feel instantly.

631
00:29:48,510 --> 00:29:51,371
You need to spend time
with a person first,

632
00:29:51,403 --> 00:29:54,468
get to know them before you
can say you love them.

633
00:29:55,993 --> 00:29:57,070
Right, Orb?

634
00:30:00,413 --> 00:30:02,380
But it seems like your
type is… someone else.

635
00:30:05,326 --> 00:30:06,632
- Dad…
- Mmm?

636
00:30:06,970 --> 00:30:08,270
I think I like someone else.

637
00:30:09,327 --> 00:30:10,262
Someone else?

638
00:30:10,287 --> 00:30:11,335
Who?

639
00:30:15,496 --> 00:30:16,569
My daughter likes you.

640
00:30:16,594 --> 00:30:19,042
- What?!
- You should marry her instead!

641
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:20,041
What?! No! No way!

642
00:30:20,066 --> 00:30:21,374
Hey!

643
00:30:22,451 --> 00:30:24,564
Wait, wait! What’s happening?!

644
00:30:39,724 --> 00:30:43,820
That’s it, Lola Maxi, don’t be sad.

645
00:30:44,494 --> 00:30:45,787
Everything’s fine now!

646
00:30:46,323 --> 00:30:52,631
You know, I’m really sorry to all of
you. Especially you, Iskineport and Chard.

647
00:30:53,871 --> 00:30:56,972
Because of me, you were accused.

648
00:30:57,194 --> 00:30:59,788
It’s just… My eyesight
isn’t what it used to be.

649
00:31:00,118 --> 00:31:01,468
Lola Maxi, we understand.

650
00:31:02,035 --> 00:31:04,608
Oh my God, I just shampooed my hair!

651
00:31:05,825 --> 00:31:08,852
Lola Maxi, you know what?
Don’t be sad, don’t worry about it.

652
00:31:09,390 --> 00:31:11,023
You should just be the
one to pay our salaries.

653
00:31:12,015 --> 00:31:14,555
That way, we’ll get
even bigger paychecks!

654
00:31:14,580 --> 00:31:17,975
Right?! We’ll be loaded!

655
00:31:18,739 --> 00:31:22,539
Wait, my love, right? What a day!

656
00:31:22,576 --> 00:31:23,909
Yeah, what a day!

657
00:31:23,934 --> 00:31:26,319
- What a day!
- What a day!

658
00:31:26,344 --> 00:31:29,334
- What a day!
- Tash! What a day, right?

659
00:31:30,369 --> 00:31:34,303
You can’t just judge people
at first glance because

660
00:31:34,342 --> 00:31:37,960
you might be wrong.
you get what I’m saying?

661
00:31:38,524 --> 00:31:41,658
What if you saw things the wrong
way? What if you misinterpreted it?

662
00:31:42,011 --> 00:31:44,184
Look at what
happened—everything got messy.

663
00:31:45,209 --> 00:31:46,576
Do you get what I’m saying?

664
00:31:46,601 --> 00:31:48,082
- Yes!
- Exactly, right?

665
00:31:48,107 --> 00:31:49,090
Possibly, right?

666
00:31:49,115 --> 00:31:52,273
You have to take a step back
and think before you judge.

667
00:31:52,298 --> 00:31:54,211
Otherwise, things just get out of control.

668
00:31:54,236 --> 00:31:58,162
Yeah! Good thing the
Three Kings didn’t mistake the

669
00:31:58,186 --> 00:32:02,113
star for something else
back then, right, my love?

670
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:03,560
Alright, here we go.

671
00:32:03,585 --> 00:32:04,270
Here we go again…

672
00:32:04,347 --> 00:32:07,453
Nice segue, you went straight to the star.

673
00:32:07,513 --> 00:32:08,073
Of course!

674
00:32:08,098 --> 00:32:08,924
Do you even know what a "tala" is?

675
00:32:09,046 --> 00:32:10,233
Of course! Do you?

676
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:11,612
A star.

677
00:32:11,637 --> 00:32:12,617
- Wow!
- Star.

678
00:32:12,642 --> 00:32:13,726
Star.

679
00:32:15,287 --> 00:32:17,480
No, but you know, on a more serious note…

680
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:18,463
Whoa!

681
00:32:18,488 --> 00:32:26,655
Really, it’s a good thing they followed
the star so they could find baby Jesus.

682
00:32:27,225 --> 00:32:32,819
And because they followed the star, they
must’ve gone through a lot of challenges.

683
00:32:33,199 --> 00:32:39,692
Just like us, when we look up and follow
God’s guidance, we go through trials.

684
00:32:40,220 --> 00:32:40,973
Yes!

685
00:32:40,998 --> 00:32:41,946
- That’s right!
- That’s right!

686
00:32:41,971 --> 00:32:48,340
That’s probably why the parol
became a symbol of Christmas.

687
00:32:49,672 --> 00:32:50,146
Mmmm!

688
00:32:50,171 --> 00:32:52,572
That’s right!

689
00:32:55,344 --> 00:32:56,697
Right, right.

690
00:32:56,795 --> 00:32:59,314
But the most important thing is,
no matter what problems come

691
00:32:59,339 --> 00:33:01,945
our way, we can overcome
them as long as we stick together.

692
00:33:02,070 --> 00:33:04,697
Right? Pers family…

693
00:33:05,417 --> 00:33:12,355
Through problems and joy,
Pers comes first, Pers is the star!

694
00:33:15,271 --> 00:33:16,731
Wait, wait, wait!

695
00:33:16,756 --> 00:33:17,231
What?

696
00:33:17,256 --> 00:33:20,786
Speaking of sticking together,
I just want to thank Dad,

697
00:33:21,572 --> 00:33:29,327
Mom, Lola Maxi, Tso K—thank you
all so much for never leaving my side.

698
00:33:29,434 --> 00:33:31,680
Of course, sweetheart!

699
00:33:31,998 --> 00:33:35,126
Most importantly, thank you, Orb.

700
00:33:42,419 --> 00:33:45,769
Of course, there’s no way I’d
let you marry someone else!

701
00:33:47,693 --> 00:33:48,767
Oh, my god!

702
00:33:53,380 --> 00:33:54,600
Why are you blushing?!

703
00:33:55,131 --> 00:33:56,372
Andres, what’s going on?

704
00:33:56,397 --> 00:33:57,936
Do you want her
for yourself now?!

705
00:33:58,353 --> 00:34:01,440
I’m telling you, stay
away from my niece!

706
00:34:02,091 --> 00:34:03,657
What, is she next?!

707
00:34:03,890 --> 00:34:06,790
- No way! Do you think this is funny?!
- Calm down, calm down…

708
00:34:07,915 --> 00:34:10,468
Don’t be mad. BFF, don’t get mad.

709
00:34:13,194 --> 00:34:16,991
Yeah, I’m not. But why do I feel this way?

710
00:34:17,016 --> 00:34:19,752
Just let the kids be. Let them be.

711
00:34:20,847 --> 00:34:23,434
Unbelievable. Okay, fine.

712
00:34:23,459 --> 00:34:27,816
- Alright, are we lighting the parol now?
- Yeah! Yeah! Okay! Okay!

713
00:34:27,849 --> 00:34:33,522
No, wait, let’s turn off all the lights
so we can really see the parol shine!

714
00:34:33,547 --> 00:34:34,521
Okay!

715
00:34:35,352 --> 00:34:36,373
Yes!

716
00:34:38,929 --> 00:34:40,037
Watch this!

717
00:34:41,500 --> 00:34:42,357
Oh!

718
00:34:42,819 --> 00:34:44,619
Wow!

719
00:34:46,105 --> 00:34:48,725
Ensaymada, finally! It’s done!

720
00:34:48,750 --> 00:34:50,195
uys, ready?

721
00:34:54,624 --> 00:34:58,817
It’s Christmas! It’s Christmas!

722
00:35:05,990 --> 00:35:11,595
Lola Maxi’s bibingka has always been a
Christmas tradition in Barangay Singko.

723
00:35:11,620 --> 00:35:13,851
We have to keep the
Christmas spirit alive in

724
00:35:13,875 --> 00:35:16,106
the barangay, just like
Lola Maxi’s bibingka.

725
00:35:16,131 --> 00:35:16,979
Secret Santa time!

726
00:35:17,004 --> 00:35:18,330
Something soft!

727
00:35:18,355 --> 00:35:19,752
- What’s that?
- Twenty pesos?

728
00:35:19,777 --> 00:35:20,833
A twenty.

729
00:35:23,922 --> 00:35:25,502
What are you doing?

730
00:35:25,527 --> 00:35:28,639
No one said you were the only
ones allowed to sell bibingka.

731
00:35:28,664 --> 00:35:29,692
Merry Christmas!

732
00:35:29,717 --> 00:35:30,931
Oh, not now, okay?

733
00:35:30,956 --> 00:35:32,335
Oh, you’re caroling?

734
00:35:32,381 --> 00:35:35,168
I hope your store makes lots of money.

735
00:35:35,193 --> 00:35:35,912
Hey, kid!

736
00:35:35,963 --> 00:35:36,742
Give him ten.

737
00:35:36,767 --> 00:35:37,983
20!

738
00:35:38,042 --> 00:35:39,069
50!

739
00:35:39,094 --> 00:35:40,544
Give him a hundred.

740
00:35:40,569 --> 00:35:41,837
We won!

741
00:35:41,914 --> 00:35:43,714
That kid scammed you!

742
00:35:43,739 --> 00:35:45,918
I have a feeling Francis
is his secret santa.

743
00:35:45,950 --> 00:35:47,380
Are you jealous?

744
00:35:47,734 --> 00:35:48,742
- Hey!
- Oh!

745
00:35:48,767 --> 00:35:49,573
- Are you hurt?
- My hand.

746
00:35:49,598 --> 00:35:50,703
Are you okay?
